<title>GERMANY: Viag sees slow non-European growth.</title>
<headline>Viag sees slow non-European growth.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Monday that it saw little chance of any dramatic expansion in its non-European international business in the short-term.</p>
<p>At the same time, a spokeswoman for Viag confirmed that the group still targets a doubling of its share of current turnover in the non-European sector.</p>
<p>Viag sales in 1996 were 42.5 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
